# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/ship-4 window (the combined ship candidate; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/ship-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-ship-4/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# SR (AFTER THE OWNER APPROVES, on the image B1 builds): the four-card platform replay of the PRODUCTION image: the node agent's serving sequence in a copy of its container
# running the THIN LAYER built on the B0 image (C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer: the step reads the image name from a file the operator writes on the runner; it is never
# committed). The replay sets no profile, so it boots the ship profile BY THE IMAGE DEFAULT, which is why it needs the baked B0 image and so the APPROVED decision. THE
# RECORDED SOURCE IMAGE: the replay copies the node agent's container from a tracked record (scripts/ci/references/c2-serving, the step's --source) and, to subtract the
# source image's own ENV from the recorded one, needs that image present on the rig host (c2_platform_replay.source_problem); when the step reports 'the source image ... is
# not on this host', the operator pulls it first (the w2-er SR needed this after the daemon had dropped it) - the image name stays out of this file. READ the vLLM
# subprocess log: '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4: vLLM argv', the OWNER TRAFFIC WAIVER line, the P150x4 mesh, admission
# passed with no UNQUALIFIED admission line and no 262k evidence waiver, prefix installed, the Lever N install and warm lines, the parked build line, every op-fusion
# lever's engaged line, the :tt alias before and after the restart, and no kill-switch line (no levern.off, prefix-reuse.off or parked.off left on the hub). PASS:
# 'PLATFORM_REPLAY passed=True'. The replay turns the session cap off; the cap is read live after the deploy. The replay step has no telemetry sidecar. Measured basis: 25
# minutes. OCTO READ (tp4/octo-3, the shape and its three levers run under this profile's waiver): python3 scripts/ci/octo_judge.py --container-log <container log>
# --profile <ship profile> clean, i.e. exactly one '[OCTO] admitted mode=live ... (owner traffic waiver <id>)' line; the six '[OCTO] UNQUALIFIED' lines, which are EXPECTED
# here (they are the card questions the waiver stands in for: the 'no UNQUALIFIED admission line' of an SR read applies to the 262k evidence waiver, not to them); at least
# 16 rounds with shape=octo at 8 live and rows=8 and no program compiled on the first octo round; the octo draft engaged once and serving at least half of the octo rounds
# at 8 live with no fallback or disabled line; the bundled attention engaged once with its call line; the glue8 engaged lines at users=8 rows=8 for every site and no
# fell-back line; the K/V page writer's 'octo 8-row served path' line once; the TAP window lever's engaged line and no fell-back line. concurrent8_steady is the test that
# supplies the octo rounds (the skew, stall and drain shapes run below six live seats most of the time). TIER READ (tp4/prefix-tiers on this profile): the host tier's
# attach lines in the container log ('[PINDIAG] prefix: host tier on', 'host tier IO attached', 'tenant quota' absent: the quotas are not in this profile), 'host tier
# restore' and 'host tier spill' lines in the tier pair's logs, no 'latched off' or failure line. Duration (estimate): 30 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-4
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=local:thin-layer
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s4
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
